House on Chicken Legs (15 seconds — comedic dieselpunk)

GLOBAL STYLE

Painterly dieselpunk aesthetic
Rust + bolts + dangling ropes + dusty ground
Exaggerated but physically grounded mech motion
Cartoony timing; no rubber limbs
Camera always moving (tiny pans, dolly drifts, hand-held wobble during chaos)

SFX

Metal creaks, servo whines, steam blasts, comedic footstep thumps, annoyed grumbling

📽️ VIDEO SCRIPT (15 seconds)
(0.0–1.0s) — COLD OPEN / CHAOTIC START

Wide shot of the wasteland.
Suddenly the mech bursts past the frame, stomping quickly, almost like it’s late for work.
Dust clouds and loose scrap fly behind it.
SFX: “THUMP-THUMP-THUMP-THUMP!”

(1.0–3.0s) — OWNER ENTRANCE

Cut to a frantic person on the ground waving arms.
They yell upward:
“HEY! STOP WALKING AWAY AGAIN!”
Camera hand-held shaky like the person is running after it.
SFX: distant metal creaks, panting, little tinkling bolts falling.

(3.0–5.5s) — MECH GUILT MOMENT

Cut to the mech freezing mid-step.
One leg is awkwardly lifted, toes curled inward.
The whole machine slowly tilts its main “body” down as if looking guilty.
One tiny window shutters close nervously.
SFX: scrawny servo whine + embarrassed creaking

(5.5–7.5s) — AWKWARD SHUFFLE

The mech slowly lowers its leg back to the ground…
and shuffles sideways like a huge embarrassed chicken.
Ropes sway, antennas twitch, steam puffs out like sighs.
SFX: “thump… scrape… thump…”

(7.5–10.0s) — OWNER SCOLDING

Lower camera angle, owner pointing finger up.
Owner: “I told you!
YOU STAY when I’m fixing your plumbing!”
Cut to mech POV: looking down at the human, slight fisheye exaggeration for comedy.

(10.0–12.5s) — LITTLE REBELLION

Close-up of a tiny hatch.
A small mechanical hand slowly pushes out and gives a tiny “shrug.”
Inside lights flicker like a silent “who, me?”
SFX: tiny metallic “tink!”

(12.5–14.0s) — FINAL SIGHT GAG

The mech tip-toes away, absurdly soft giant footsteps.
Every step lifts exaggeratedly high like a sneaking cartoon character.
Behind it, a rope ladder swings wildly.

(14.0–15.0s) — END CARD

Camera whip-pan to a dusty sign planted in the ground:

“SMART HOMES ARE GETTING OUT OF CONTROL.”
A metal boot from the mech quietly sneaks into frame like it’s photobombing.

Fade out with a comedic boing-clank.